INSERT INTO posts (title, slug, excerpt, content, category, coverImage, news_beat, published, featured) SELECT 'Kyiv attacks put scientific institutions and civilian life under renewed strain', 'kyiv-attacks-put-scientific-institutions-and-civilian-life-under-renewed-strain-2026-09-29', 'Reports dated September 28–29 describe damage at the National Academy of Sciences and pressure on air defenses.', '## Ukraine brief · September 29, 2026
Reuters reported a September 28 Russian attack that damaged Ukraine''s National Academy of Sciences in central Kyiv. Its September 29 follow-up described a scientist escaping the burning building. The accounts show how war can reach institutions whose work extends far beyond a battlefield.

Associated Press separately reported increasing pressure from ballistic missiles and faster drones, alongside shortages of air-defense interceptors. Assessments of military capability can change and are not a forecast that any particular city will be protected or struck.

## Continuing coverage
This desk will follow civilian disruption, scientific and cultural institutions, energy infrastructure and diplomatic developments. We will attribute battlefield claims and update casualty figures with their source and time rather than treating an early number as final.

## Sources
- [Reuters: scientist escapes academy attack](https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/trapped-inferno-after-russian-strike-ukrainian-scientist-climbed-safety-2026-09-29/)
- [Associated Press: Kyiv air-defense pressures](https://apnews.com/article/aceadaec18c41244dc6e9d17732ba256)

